@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
    ViewData["BodyClass"] = "dn-inner";
}

<div class="container py-4 py-md-5 dn-page">
    <header class="mb-4 pb-3 border-bottom border-opacity-10">
        <p class="dn-page-eyebrow mb-0">Legal</p>
        <h1 class="dn-page-title mb-2">Privacy &amp; data</h1>
        <p class="dn-page-lead mb-0">How Diagnova treats information in this demo / coursework build. Replace with counsel-reviewed text before any public launch.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="dn-surface-card dn-surface-card-lg p-4 p-md-5 dn-prose">
        <h2>What we store</h2>
        <p>
            Accounts use ASP.NET Core Identity with a local SQLite database. Chat sessions, messages, and vitals you submit are tied to your user id and kept on the server this app runs on.
        </p>

        <h2>Third parties</h2>
        <p>
            Medicine pages may call the U.S. FDA OpenFDA API. The symptom assistant may call an OpenAI-compatible API when configured. Those providers have their own privacy policies and retention rules.
        </p>

        <h2>AI disclaimer</h2>
        <p>
            Assistant output is generated and may be wrong or incomplete. It is not medical diagnosis or treatment. Do not rely on it for emergencies.
        </p>

        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <p>
            You can stop using the app, delete local database files in development, or extend this page with export and account-deletion flows as your project evolves.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
